/* Deep lessons — Math va number theory (math).
 *
 * The track where formulas usually arrive without their reasons. Here every
 * one of them is built before it is written: modular arithmetic on a circle,
 * Euclid's algorithm as a rectangle peeled into squares, binomials as a
 * triangle, inclusion-exclusion as overlapping discs, a sieve as a grid being
 * struck out.
 *
 * The rule throughout: if a learner cannot say WHY a formula is true, they
 * will misapply it under contest pressure. So nothing is stated that is not
 * also derived, and every derivation is small enough to redo on paper.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

